---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="教學｜王雅萍 Ong Nga Ping"
  description="國立政治大學民族學系王雅萍副教授歷年授課與教學資訊"
>
  <main class="teaching-page">

    <!-- =====================================================
         PAGE HEADER
    ====================================================== -->

    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">TEACHING</p>

      <h1>
        <span data-lang="zh">教學</span>
        <span data-lang="en">Teaching</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="intro">
        <span data-lang="zh">
          王雅萍副教授的教學涵蓋民族與原住民族教育、
          臺灣民族史、民族學研究方法、東南亞研究、
          社區發展、地方創生與社會實踐等領域。
        </span>

        <span data-lang="en">
          Associate Professor Ong Nga Ping's teaching covers
          ethnic and Indigenous education, ethnic history of Taiwan,
          research methods in ethnology, Southeast Asian studies,
          community development, placemaking, and social engagement.
        </span>
      </p>

      <p class="data-note">
        <span data-lang="zh">
          主要課程以 110–114 學年度（2021–2026）
          至少跨三個學年重複開設之課程或相關課程群整理。
        </span>

        <span data-lang="en">
          Core courses are identified from courses or closely related
          course groups offered across at least three academic years
          between Academic Years 110–114 (2021–2026).
        </span>
      </p>
    </header>


    <!-- =====================================================
         CORE COURSES
    ====================================================== -->

    <section>
      <p class="section-label">CORE COURSES · 2021–2026</p>

      <h2>
        <span data-lang="zh">近五年主要課程</span>
        <span data-lang="en">Core Courses in Recent Years</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="core-courses">

        <!-- 01 臺灣民族史 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">01</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">五學年持續開設</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Offered across all five academic years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">臺灣民族史</span>
            <span data-lang="en">History of Ethnos in Taiwan</span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            110-1 · 111-2 · 112-1 · 113-1 · 114-1
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              從家鄉與地方的民族分布出發，以多民族視角理解臺灣歷史，
              探討不同歷史時期的族群關係、原住民族歷史事件、
              地方史、民族史與國家史，並結合檔案、文化場館與校外踏查。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Beginning with the ethnic composition of local communities,
              the course approaches Taiwan's history from a multi-ethnic
              perspective. It examines ethnic relations, Indigenous histories,
              local history, ethnic history, and national history through
              archival materials, cultural institutions, and field visits.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>


        <!-- 02 民族教育 / 原住民族教育 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">02</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">五學年持續開設</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Continuously represented across five years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">
              民族教育／原住民族教育
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Ethnic Education / Indigenous Education
            </span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            110-1 · 110-2 · 111-2 · 112-1 · 112-2 ·
            113-2 · 114-1 · 115-1
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              從教育經驗、民族文化與教育制度出發，
              探討民族教育與原住民族教育的政策、法規、理論及教育現場。
              課程亦回應「全民原教」的發展，
              並與原住民族師資培育及族語教育相連結。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              These courses examine ethnic and Indigenous education through
              educational experience, cultural diversity, policy, law,
              theory, and educational practice. They also address the
              development of Indigenous education for all citizens and its
              connections with teacher education and Indigenous language
              education.
            </span>
          </p>

          <p class="course-note">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              ※「民族教育」與「原住民族教育」為不同正式課名，
              此處依近年相連的教學主軸合併呈現。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              ※ “Ethnic Education” and “Indigenous Education” are
              distinct official course titles and are grouped here because
              of their closely connected teaching focus.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>


        <!-- 03 社會企業 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">03</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">連續四學年</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Four consecutive academic years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">社會企業專題</span>
            <span data-lang="en">Seminar in Social Enterprise</span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            111-1 · 112-1 · 113-1 · 114-1
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              從政府、企業與民間社會之間的公私協力關係出發，
              探討社會企業如何回應快速變遷的社會、經濟與環境問題，
              並思考公共服務、組織自主性、社會價值與永續發展。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              The course examines social enterprise through partnerships
              among government, business, and civil society. It considers
              how social enterprises respond to social, economic, and
              environmental challenges while creating public and social value.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>


        <!-- 04 地方創生 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">04</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">近五年多次開設</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Repeatedly offered in recent years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">
              地方創生與青年創業實驗室
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Lab for Placemaking and Youth Startup
            </span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            110-2 · 113-2 · 114-2
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              以地方人口流失、產業發展、人口老化及城鄉差距等議題為背景，
              透過地方創生、青年返鄉與創業、社區發展和實作學習，
              引導學生從真實地方問題發展行動方案。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Focusing on population loss, regional inequality,
              aging communities, and local industries, the course uses
              placemaking, youth entrepreneurship, community development,
              and action-based learning to explore solutions to local issues.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>


        <!-- 05 社區資源管理 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">05</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">跨三學年開設</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Offered across three academic years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">
              以社區為本的文化資源管理：
              台灣與泰國的經驗對話
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Community-based Social and Cultural Resources Management:
              Taiwan and Thailand Experiences
            </span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            110-1 · 112-2 · 113-2
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              比較臺灣與泰國的社區文化資源管理政策與案例，
              涵蓋社區發展、原住民族文化健康、地方創生與生態知識，
              並透過跨國教師、案例及田野參訪建立臺泰經驗對話。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              This course compares community-based cultural resource
              management in Taiwan and Thailand, covering community
              development, Indigenous cultural and health practices,
              placemaking, ecological knowledge, international dialogue,
              and field-based case studies.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>


        <!-- 06 研究方法 -->

        <article class="course-card">
          <div class="course-meta">
            <span class="course-number">06</span>

            <span class="frequency">
              <span data-lang="zh">連續三學年</span>
              <span data-lang="en">Three consecutive academic years</span>
            </span>
          </div>

          <h3>
            <span data-lang="zh">研究方法與個案分析</span>
            <span data-lang="en">Research Methods and Case Analysis</span>
          </h3>

          <p class="semesters">
            110-1 · 111-1 · 112-1
          </p>

          <p class="course-description">
            <span data-lang="zh">
              以質性研究方法為核心，涵蓋研究方法論、
              民族誌研究、個案與文獻回顧、研究問題形成、
              方法設計及研究計畫撰寫，讓學生從實作中建立研究能力。
            </span>

            <span data-lang="en">
              Centered on qualitative research, the course covers
              methodology, ethnography, case analysis, literature review,
              research-question development, research design, and the
              preparation of a research proposal.
            </span>
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


